    "title": "NBA fans react to incredible Cooper Flagg training camp footage - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Divij Kulkarni ,\n3 hours ago\nOne of the most exciting things for NBA fans going into the 2025-26 season is an opportunity to finally watch Cooper Flagg play basketball at the highest level. The No. 1 overall pick from Duke, Flagg is one of the most hyped prospects in recent memory. He impressed during Summer League, but that doesn’t mean much in terms of how he’ll do in the league.\nFlagg is on the Dallas Mavericks, who received the No. 1 overall pick against all odds in the 2025 NBA Draft Lottery. He reported for his first day of training camp this week, with only a few weeks left for the regular season to begin. And as soon as the Mavs released footage of the rookie in training, fans had a lot to say about it on social media.\nRELATED: Former WNBA All-Star denies Kevin Durant dating rumors\n“Mavs fans are eating good this season, he looks great goddamn,” one fan wrote. “I said y’all should bookmark this, Dallas Mavericks are winning this season,” another fan said.\n“The league is shaking rn, the kid’s a monster,” a third fan commented. “How you gonna walk in on your first day and block AD man, he’s too special,” said a fourth fan.\nDallas Mavericks forward C poses for a photo during the Mavericks’ 2025 media day at the American Airlines Center. Mandatory Credit: Jerome Miron-Imagn Images “Boy, him and AD might go stoopid on defense if AD can stay healthy,” a fifth fan observed. “Watching a minute of practice highlights has never gotten me so irrationally excited,” claimed a sixth fan.\nDespite not having played even a minute in an NBA game yet, Flagg has turned fans into believers already. For a city and a franchise reeling from the Luka Doncic trade, Cooper could prove to be a godsend. If he lives up to his hype, the rest of the Western Conference might just be in trouble sooner than they realize.\nGET MORE TOP STORIES from The Big Lead by subscribing to TBL YouTube channel\nWEDNESDAY ROUNDUP: Dodgers drum Reds to kick off MLB postseason, Browns ready for change, and more\nNFL: Head coaches on the hot seat entering Week 5 of the NFL season\nNBA: League insider suggests Adam Silver isn’t neutral in LA Clippers investigation\nNCAAF: Colorado receives hefty fine from Big 12 for ‘inappropriate chants’ during BYU game\nWNBA: Lynx star Napheesa Collier goes scorched earth on WNBA commissioner Cathy Engelbert\nVIRAL: Kevin Durant shoots his shot with Kay Adams with Rockets game, BBQ invite\nThe post NBA fans react to incredible Cooper Flagg training camp footage appeared first on The Big Lead .",
